    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d31">

                <pb facs="0083" n="39" sameAs="frus:frus1952-54v05p1/pg39"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Conference files, lot 59 D 95. CF 102</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum of Conversation, by Lucius D. Battle </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">confidential</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" type="conversation-or-meeting-date"
                            when="1952-02-14">February 14, 1952</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>During a conversation on other matters, Mr. Churchill mentioned the proposed move
                    of the NATO Headquarters from London to Paris. The Secretary said he made a very
                    vigorous speech to Mr. Churchill regarding this problem and that Mr. Churchill
                    was a little surprised and hard-up for answers on points which the Secretary
                    made in which he urged the Headquarters be moved to Paris.</p>
            </div>
